quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  17,28,"And if you have to overlook them (for their lack of means), seeking the mercy of your Lord, which you will (soon) expect, then (at least) speak to them a gentle word."
  17,29,"Do not keep your hand chained to your neck (i.e. do not be miserly), nor open it all together (i.e. do not overspend), lest you sit down blamed, regretful."
  17,30,"Indeed, your Lord expands the provision for whom He wishes and straitens (it for whom He wills). Surely, He is All-Aware, All-Seeing of His servants."
  17,31,"And do not kill your children fearing poverty. We provide for them and for you. Indeed, their killing is a great sin."
  17,32,And do not go near adultery. It is an indecent act and an evil path.
  17,33,"And do not kill any soul whom Allah has forbidden, except lawfully. And whoever is killed unjustly, We have certainly given his heir the authority (of obtaining legal retribution). But he must not commit any excess in (the retributive) killing, for he indeed enjoys the support (of the Law)."
  17,34,"And do not go near the orphan’s property, except in the most virtuous manner, until he attains maturity. And fulfil the promise. Indeed, all promises are accountable."
  17,35,"Give full measure when you measure, and weigh with an accurate scale. That is better and more virtuous in outcome."
  17,36,"And do not follow (blindly) what you do not know (to be the truth). Indeed, the hearing, the seeing and the heart—all of these shall be held accountable."
  17,37,"And do not walk proudly on the earth. Indeed, you can neither tear up the earth nor reach the mountains in height."
  17,38,The evil of all these (actions) is detestable in the sight of your Lord.
